      "side": 1,
      "message": "The TUSB1064 may be configured either via hardware pin straps, or software register setting.\n\nIn ServoV4p1, the chip is left in hardware-managed floating mode. This code was intended to remove that ambiguity and place the chip in a software-known state explicitly. Not just at boot, but at any re-init.\n\nI agree this could be split into a separate call if a hypothetical hardware engineer resistor straps the pins to another value intentionally, and ignores the software. However -- HW changes still requires SW review; SW changes may be HW agnostic (or infeasible to review).\n\nI defer to more experienced bringup and maintenance experts regarding proper approach.",
